<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A delivery motorbike costs Ksh <m>{240\,000}</m>. Give a yearly rate of depreciation (reducing balance) for which it is worth less than half its price after <m>{3}</m> years, but not after <m>{2}</m> years. Many answers are correct; you may use one decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ansr"/> %  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Half the price is Ksh <m>{120\,000}</m>. Try a rate and work out the value after <m>{2}</m> and after <m>{3}</m> years.</p><p>For example, with <m>{25}\%</m> the multiplier is <m>{0.75}</m>: after <m>{2}</m> years the value is Ksh <m>{135\,000}</m>, still at least half, and after <m>{3}</m> years Ksh <m>{101\,250}</m>, below half. So <m>{25}\%</m> works.</p><p>By trial, to one decimal place the rates that work are from <m>{20.7}\%</m> to <m>{29.2}\%</m>. A smaller rate is too slow; a bigger rate takes the value below half a year too early.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>25</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>